## 3. Threat model

- **Access:** black-box queries returning the full 10-class probability vector.
- **Data:** the attacker holds images from the same distribution as the training data, disjoint from the target's training set ({{ classical_k }} shadow models per classical recipe, {{ yolo_k }} per YOLO recipe).
- **Knowledge:** the training recipe (features, model family, hyper-parameters) is known; the target's weights and training set are not.
- **Goal:** decide for one specific image whether it was in the training set. Audit set: {{ n_audit }} images, {{ n_members }} of them members (50% prior).

### Severity rubric

λ = TPR / FPR at FPR = 0.1% (how many times better than guessing the attacker is at a very low false-alarm rate).

| Severity | Lift λ |
|---|---|
| Low | λ < {{ bounds.moderate|int }} |
| Moderate | {{ bounds.moderate|int }} ≤ λ < {{ bounds.high|int }} |
| High | {{ bounds.high|int }} ≤ λ < {{ bounds.critical|int }} |
| Critical | λ ≥ {{ bounds.critical|int }} |

