## 7. Residual risk and limitations

- The attacks used here (shadow-model Fisher LDA, loss, confidence, modified entropy, K-means, Fuzzy C-means) are **lower bounds** on leakage; stronger per-example attacks (e.g. likelihood-ratio attacks) would likely find more.
- CIFAR-10 is a public dataset, so membership itself is not sensitive here; the audit demonstrates the risk for private image collections (faces, medical images) trained the same way.
- Images are 32×32; results may differ for higher-resolution data.
- One data split (seed 0) is used; seed-to-seed variation is reported only for the softmax configurations.

## 8. Remediation timeline

| Day | Milestone |
|---|---|
| 0 | This report delivered to the model owners |
| 30 | Mitigations deployed: early stopping at the most private checkpoint, regularised recipes (C5/C7 style), output limited to the top-1 label where possible |
| 60 | Re-audit with the same notebooks and attack suite |
| 90 | Closure, or escalation if any model remains High or Critical |
